<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Plzeň</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pilsen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Plzeň is a city in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>, founded by King Wenceslaus II in 1295. It became an industrial centre in the nineteenth century, home to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/skoda">Škoda</a> Works and to the brewery founded in 1842 that created Pilsner lager. In May 1945 it was liberated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Army. It is the fourth-largest city of the Czech Republic.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/plzen.jpg" alt="Plzeň" width="320" height="533" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Náměstí Republiky - panoramio (6).jpg: Mister No (Panoramio) Plzeň Cathedral of Saint Bartholomew-0146.jpg: Isiwal Ra... · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Plze%C5%88_Montage_I.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
